# Document changes in Obsidian

After any meaningful change (feature, refactor, upgrade, bugfix, config, infra, decision), update `hookio-vault/` before ending the session. Do not invent another vault.

| Kind | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Index / MOC | `Hookio.md` |
| Changelog | `Hookio/Changelog.md` (newest first) |
| Infrastructure | `Hookio/Infrastructure.md` |
| Service | `Hookio/Services/<name>.md` |
| Feature | `Hookio/Features/<name>.md` |
| Decision | `Hookio/Decisions/<short-name>.md` |
| Convention | `Hookio/How we document.md` |

Update the existing service/feature note plus the changelog. Do not create a `Plans/` folder or “do this next” sequences. Do not duplicate notes.

Changelog and decisions: Date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), What, Why, Files / packages, Follow-ups, PR if any.

Example: changing EventSub HMAC → update `Hookio/Services/Twitch.md` and `Hookio/Features/Twitch EventSub.md`, then add a newest-first changelog entry.

Skip typos and formatting-only edits unless they encode a decision.
